  "slug": "biomolecular-modeling-context-parallelism-9c87",
  "summary": "Large assemblies and cryo-EM workflows are driving GPU-scale parallelization and accelerated inference across three recent preprints.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is GPU-level engineering that removes throughput limits in biomolecular modeling, applied to structure prediction and cryo-EM reconstruction. Fold-CP distributes co-folding model inference and training across GPUs using context parallelism, enabling structure prediction of assemblies over 30,000 in size. OpenFold-TRT pairs TensorRT-accelerated OpenFold inference with MMseqs2-GPU homology search, reporting up to 131x speedup over AlphaFold2. torch-projectors is a differentiable PyTorch Fourier-projection library for cryo-EM single-particle and tomography workflows, reported as 1-2 orders faster than torch-fourier-slice. What is new is the shift from algorithmic novelty toward parallelization, runtime optimization, and differentiable GPU-native implementations within standard deep learning frameworks. All three are preprints, so the reported speedups and scaling figures await peer review. torch-projectors addresses a different modality from the two structure-prediction tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-03-16"
}
